Myth: In a desert of glass and wind, there stood a wellspring keeper named Nyra who bottled moments instead of water. Each dawn, she uncorked a sliver of memory and poured it into the air, letting time soften the heat and settle into the bones of travelers. The dunes listened, shifting with gratitude as voices found footing again, and the sun learned to temper its blaze with whispered histories.

